    text:"Cohere and Aleph Alpha signed a definitive combination agreement Sept. 16, formalizing the merger the two companies first disclosed in April. The combined company will operate globally as Cohere, dual-headquartered in Berlin and Toronto, valued at roughly $20 billion, with Germany's Schwarz Group committing $600 million to Cohere's upcoming Series E.",
    why:"A transatlantic merger between two mid-tier sovereign/enterprise-AI labs, each too small alone to compete with the frontier labs on compute, is a concrete bet that scale consolidation below the top tier is starting now rather than waiting for a shakeout.",
    heat:37, topics:["cohere","aleph alpha","merger","enterprise ai","funding","germany","canada"],
